  r3d:description "The CATH database is a hierarchical domain classification of protein structures in the Protein Data Bank. Protein structures are classified using a combination of automated and manual procedures.  There are four major levels in the CATH hierarchy; Class, Architecture, Topology and Homologous superfamily."@eng ;
